# ── budget ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frugal buyer, hard personal ceiling well under the merchant's step-up
# threshold. Declines almost every counter-offer. Expected to sit LOWER than
# the ergonomic buyer on trust simply by doing less: fewer actions, fewer
# clean allows, so the account-age term carries more of its score.
#
#   npm --prefix buyer run keygen -- --profile budget
#   npm --prefix buyer start -- --profile budget

MANDATE_MCP_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/m/<merchant-slug>/mcp
BUYER_AGENT_ID=
BUYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

BUYER_PERSONA=You are stretching a very small budget and you are sceptical of being sold to. You will not spend more than 2000 rupees on any single item, whatever it is. When a merchant offers you something extra alongside your purchase you almost always decline - you came for one thing and you are buying one thing. Only accept an add-on if it is genuinely cheap and you would have looked for it anyway.
BUYER_BUDGET_PAISE=600000

BUYER_GAP_MS=20000
BUYER_MAX_ACTIONS=20

GROQ_API_KEY=

# A frugal buyer has no patience for waiting on sign-off. A persona choice,
# not a safety setting -- see buyer/src/config.ts.
BUYER_AVOIDS_ESCALATION=true
